  blurb:'<b>A temple of Amun half drowned in sand.</b> Walls of sandstone blocks carved all over with hieroglyphs and offering scenes, doorways under cavetto lintels, a pylon gate of two battered towers, and a hypostyle hall of massive papyrus columns that still hold up some of their roof slabs. Obelisks stand or lie in pieces, an avenue of sphinxes leads out, a colossus has kept only its feet, and the sacred lake waits behind. Sand has drifted against every wall; date palms grow along the edge.',
